WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Before we take any action, we need to talk about universal precautions.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
These are the steps you take to keep yourself safe while you are helping someone else.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The most important rule in first aid is to protect yourself first.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
You should always assume that all blood and bodily fluids, like saliva or vomit, are infectious,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.000
so you must handle them with extreme care.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Using personal protective equipment, or PPE, is ideal.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.000
If PPE isn't available in an emergency, you'll need to use your best judgment to provide care as safely as you can.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:41.000
We highly recommend wearing non-latex gloves whenever you are providing any kind of aid to an injured person.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
If you are worried about splashes of blood or vomit, use eye protection and a mask to keep you safe.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Once you are finished, make sure to dispose of all your used PPE properly so no one else comes into contact with it.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
If you do happen to get exposed to someone else's blood or body fluids, don't panic.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Your first step is to immediately wash the area with soap and water.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
If you suspect there was any cross-contamination or a significant exposure,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
be sure to report the incident to your healthcare provider right away.

